de\n  fact, the constant $256 + A_t$, is quoted in the statement section\n  for its value. 02d: the Lean theorem is transcribed as a display, not\n  shown verbatim, because the house build cannot typeset its symbols.\n  08xd: Section~\\ref{sec:statement} says the proof's constant is at\n  least 257 and the exhibited theorem's at least 258, two readings of\n  two lines, both kept.\n\\item[Beyond the statement (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}).] 03a: a third\n  tag, ``supported'', between verified and paper-only. 03c: what the\n  verified exponent would give through Corollary~1.4's argument is not\n  worked out. 03d: Corollary~1.2 is stated with the verified exponent\n  and tagged supported, not verified.\n\\item[The proof and the replay (Sections~\\ref{sec:proof} and\n  \\ref{sec:replay}).] 01b: the second checker is \\texttt{nanoda\\_lib}\n  at the commit named, with \\texttt{lean4export} at the nearest tag.\n  01c: that checker was run with the three axioms permitted and unused\n  axioms ignored. 01d: ``replayed'' means the build, the axiom output\n  and the second checker, not the comparator run. 04a: thirty-five\n  definitions compared, thirty-three identical, two up to a keyword;\n  the audit's ``33'' is explained, not kept. 04c: the exhibited\n  constants, $A \\ge 258$ and $C \\ge 28{,}701$, are stated with their\n  lines.\n\\item[What follows (Section~\\ref{sec:consequences}).] 05a: the\n  manuscript's list of problems is elided from one quotation, by the\n  paper's scope. 05b: SETH is refuted by reading the statement at each\n  width, and ``SETH implies ETH'' is cited for the record. 05c: the\n  hypotheses' sources are copied from the manuscript's reference list\n  and not re-read. 05d: two paragraphs are ours and not the\n  manuscript's, and say so.\n\\item[For the practitioner (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}).] 06a: the\n  two guarantee curves share one scale factor, so that they cross where\n  the statement puts the crossing. 06c: seven references for the tools\n  and the threshold are from memory, with no DOI checked. 06d: the\n  counters are reported at their defaults, including a plateau that\n  looks like a preprocessing budget.\n\\item[Our Lean (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}).] 07b: the axiom audit prints\n  two lines with fewer than the three axioms, and ``every line on the\n  three'' is read as ``nothing beyond the three''. 07c: the re-diff also\n  matches the restatement's body to the theorem's, beyond what was\n  asked.\n\\item[Related work (Section~\\ref{sec:related}).] 08a: the audit paper's\n  title is typeset with an apostrophe the arXiv record lacks. 08b: four\n  small public records were fetched beside the three allowed pages, for\n  their dates and commits. 08c: fourteen references carry no checked\n  DOI. 08d: ``we found no earlier statement'' is bounded to six texts.\n\\item[Plain English, and this section.] 08xa: the dense passages were\n  moved into Appendix~\\ref{app:tech}, not cut. 08xc: the glosses are\n  repeated in each section and now also in the introduction. 09a: the\n  introduction and abstract state the title's third clause in words,\n  with no formula beyond $2^n$, by the plain-English rule rather than\n  by the item's brief. 09b: the abstract carries two numbers, both from\n  Section~\\ref{sec:statement}'s script, and no count from the replay.\n  09c: this sorting of the entries into resolved, procedural and open\n  is the author's to redo. 09d: ``people who checked'' in the stance\n  sentence is read as the author and the assistant the acknowledgements\n  disclose.\n\\end{description}\n\nThirteen of the thirty-three are bibliographic or typographic (S2, 02b,\n02d, 05c, 06c, 08a, 08b, 08c and the five spelling, placement and\ntagging choices of 02a, 03a, 03d, 04a, 08xa); the rest are choices\nabout what the text says, and each is a sentence that can be struck\nwithout touching any number.\n\n\\subsection{What this does not claim}\n\\label{sec:conclusion-not}\n\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{N