{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FnCHBWtWekHErNt6JzbJ9v","type":"tool_result","content":"=== hashes.txt\nreplay copy HEAD: 4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae\npristine clone HEAD: 4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae\ngit status --short of the replay copy (tracked files): 0 lines\n\n4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685  replay/openai-math/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean\ndebbfdc9c01104d2369be80da5180978275106df8b685f693fba7ce7da7c5b19  replay/openai-math/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.json\n040360a8465957622d934e5f1bb4f2cce8dab950e78f52033fbf70da493184f5  replay/openai-math/lean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/SqrtLogSpace/Final.lean\ncbd4cebf71f1d3239c21241f946d05e8de802dbb9c138713f8e7182d868b2d1c  replay/openai-math/lean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/Main.lean\nd5edba4e4b8faad9c1baeadb265716d20d03be4d1a2647dc5e35b0c0325bea7b  replay/openai-math/lean/lean-toolchain\ncf6105a25d9dca2f166b241d9191bd12c7e13305890dc9c4d0952351cccc0794  replay/openai-math/lean/lake-manifest.json\nd313f594daa3cd3713f872bde8b4d33138820eeec5a335a21a276846aa54e21e  logs/build_main.log\n\nsame files in the pristine clone:\n4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685  lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean\ndebbfdc9c01104d2369be80da5180978275106df8b685f693fba7ce7da7c5b19  lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.json\n040360a8465957622d934e5f1bb4f2cce8dab950e78f52033fbf70da493184f5  lean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/SqrtLogSpace/Final.lean\ncbd4cebf71f1d3239c21241f946d05e8de802dbb9c138713f8e7182d868b2d1c  lean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/Main.lean\nd5edba4e4b8faad9c1baeadb265716d20d03be4d1a2647dc5e35b0c0325bea7b  lean/lean-toolchain\ncf6105a25d9dca2f166b241d9191bd12c7e13305890dc9c4d0952351cccc0794  lean/lake-manifest.json\n=== export sha\nbdbc9afe336fea99b01bc4eced6e4232153afdefe13a1095cdc5ca9499e3f573  logs/export.ndjson\n2355666449 bytes\n43633742\n=== build sha\nd313f594daa3cd3713f872bde8b4d33138820eeec5a335a21a276846aa54e21e  logs/build_main.log\n=== lean README\n# The companion Lean of paper 3\n\n*Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.*\n\nPaper 3's Section 8 (\"The statement in our Lean\"). Nothing here is a Lean\nsource file of its own beyond the audit: the companion Lean is two files of\nour library, left where loop0014 wrote them by the owner's decision of\n2026-11-05 (`paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`, S3 resolved: \"leave the Lean where it\nis\"; the original brief of item 07, which moved them to\n`lean/MOSPFormalization/ETH/`, is superseded, entry 07a).\n\n## The files\n\n| file | what it is | lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/PrimitiveMachine.lean` | a verbatim copy of lines 1–190 and 220 of `lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` in the OpenAI collection (commit `4eaee875`, SHA-256 `4183b205…`), after a 30-line header (source, commit, hash, Apache 2.0 licence). Definitions only: the formulas and their count, the canonical encoding, the multitape `PrimitiveMachine`, `Trace`, `runtimeScale` (ρ(n) = n (ln ln(n+16))² / √ln(n+16)), `runtimeBound`, `countWord`, the located configuration, `locatedStep`, `visitedSpace`. The theorem and its `sorry` (clone lines 191–219) are not copied. | 221; the copy is lines 31–221 |\n| `lean/MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean` | `SubexpCount (k : ℕ) : Prop` (lines 84–107), the comparator theorem's body character for character; `ExactCountAndSat : Prop := ∀ k, 2 ≤ k → SubexpCount k` (110); the lemmas `SubexpCount.anti` (113), `ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount` (119), `IsSubexpExponent` (125), `runtimeBound_eq` (128), `tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt` (132), `runtimeScale_isLittleO` (144), `isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale` (163), `LocatedCfg.monitor_config` (169), `Trace.config_of_locatedStep` (180). Lines 192–268 belong to the other study and are not cited by the paper. | 268 |\n\nBoth files are imported by `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean` (lines 76–77) and\nbuilt by `lake build` in `lean/`; the loop's gate checks after every session\nthat the whole library has no `sorry` and no `axiom` declaration.\n\n## The names the paper cites\n\nAppendix A of the paper (`paper3/latex/secA_appendix_lean.tex`), eight rows:\nthe copied vocabulary (ten `OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.…` names),\n`SubexpCount`, `ExactCountAndSat`, `SubexpCount.anti` with\n`ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount`, `runtimeBound_eq`, `tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt`\nwith `runtimeScale_isLittleO`, `IsSubexpExponent` with\n`isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale`, `LocatedCfg.monitor_config` with\n`Trace.config_of_locatedStep`. All under the namespace\n`MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth` except the copy, whose namespaces are the\nsource's.\n\n## The audit\n\n`axiom_check.lean` prints the axioms of those 21 declarations, in the pattern\nof `paper1/axiom_check.lean` (without its `sorryAx` control line: this paper's\nacceptance rule is that every line is on the three standard axioms, entry\n07b). Run from `lean/`:\n\n```bash\ncd lean && lake env lean ../paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean > ../paper3/lean/axiom_check.log\n```\n\n`axiom_check.log` is the committed output (2026-11-05 05:30 UTC, repository\ncommit `95eb564a0`, Lean 4.34.0-rc2 commit `6a10ac8c`, Lake 5.0.0, Mathlib\n`1192d6246b46` from `lean/lake-manifest.json` — our library's toolchain, not\nthe clone's `v4.34.1` / `d13f23b7`): 19 lines on exactly\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; `Computation.Trace` on no axiom\n(an inductive definition); `SqrtLogSpace.countWord` on `[propext, Quot.sound]`;\n`sorryAx` on none.\n\n## The re-diff\n\n`python3 -I paper3/scripts/lean_rediff.py` (from the repository root; `--check`\nverifies without writing) reads the clone with `open()` only and writes\n`rediff.log`:\n\n1. **the copy**: our lines 31–221 against the clone's lines 1–190 followed\n   by 220, byte for byte — identical (191 lines each side, diff empty); the\n   clone's SHA-256 and commit as the header records;\n2. **the statement**: the body of `SubexpCount` (Frame.lean 85–107) against\n   the body of `exact_count_and_sat` (clone 195–217, `:= by` removed) —\n   identical after whitespace normalisation (1,073 characters) and line by\n   line after stripping indentation (23 lines; ours sit two columns further\n   left, a `def` body against a `theorem` type);\n3. **no `sorry`, no `axiom`** in either of our files outside the header\n   comment; the clone's one `sorry` is at line 218, outside the copied range.\n\nExit status is non-zero if any check fails.\n\n## What this does not claim\n\n`SubexpCount k` is a `def` of a `Prop`, never proved here and never an axiom;\nthe copy is definitions only (the proof's 3,091 modules are not copied); no\n`#eval` can evaluate `runtimeScale` (it is `noncomputable`, over real\nlogarithms — every number in the paper's Section 2 is from a Python script);\nthe statement match is textual, not a `lean4export`-level check; the lemmas\nfix the shape of the bound and the limit of the exponent and say nothing\nabout any machine's running time, the constants, or the manuscript's\nunverified exponents.\n=== gate.py\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0015 (paper 3).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the papers build with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`,\n   and `make -C paper3/latex check` once paper3/latex/Makefile exists; skipped\n   with a printed note until then);\n6. nothing under solutions/ is modified, added or deleted (`git status`), and\n   paper3/latex/main.tex still carries the owner's title verbatim.\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0015/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport re\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\nPAPER3 = REPO / \"paper3\" / \"latex\"\nTITLE = (\"Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower \"\n         \"than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.\")\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef _run(cmd: list[str], cwd: Path, timeout: float) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n    \"\"\"`subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, timeout=timeout)` with two\n    differences, both from the loop0014 item 01 gate hang (2026-11-02): the\n    command runs in its own session, so that on timeout its whole process group\n    is killed (`subprocess.run` kills only the direct child, and the forked\n    pytest worker that had hung outlived the gate by an hour), and the output\n    produced before the timeout travels with the exception, so that `main` can\n    print which test was running.\"\"\"\n    proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=cwd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n                            text=True, errors=\"replace\", start_new_session=True)\n    try:\n        out, _ = proc.communicate(timeout=timeout)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n        out, _ = proc.communicate()\n        raise subprocess.TimeoutExpired(cmd, timeout, output=out)\n    return subprocess.CompletedProcess(cmd, proc.returncode, out, \"\")\n\n\n# A test that runs this long has every thread's stack dumped to stderr (pytest's\n# faulthandler plugin); the test goes on, and the dump names it if the gate\n# then times out. The suite takes about 5 min in all.\nFAULTHANDLER = \"faulthandler_timeout=900\"\n\n\ndef _main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\n    root = (LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        mod = \"MOSPFormalization.\" + \".\".join(f.relative_to(LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").with_suffix(\"\").parts)\n        if not re.search(rf\"^import {re.escape(mod)}\\s*$\", root, re.M):\n            print(f\"GATE FAIL: {mod} is not imported by MOSPFormalization.lean\"); ok = False\n\n    sorries, axioms = [], []\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        code = strip_comments(f.read_text())\n        for n, line in enumerate(code.splitlines(), 1):\n            if re.search(r\"\\bsorry\\b\", line):\n                sorries.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n            if re.match(r\"\\s*(private\\s+)?axiom\\b\", line):\n                axioms.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n    allowed = [l for l in ALLOWED.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")] if ALLOWED.exists() else []\n    limit = BASELINE_SORRIES + len(allowed)\n    print(f\"sorry in code: {len(sorries)} (limit {limit}): {sorries}\")\n    if len(sorries) > limit:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: more sorry than the baseline plus allowed_sorries.txt\"); ok = False\n    if axioms:\n        print(f\"GATE FAIL: axiom declarations: {axioms}\"); ok = False\n\n    t = _run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"tests/\", \"-q\", \"-x\", \"-o\", FAULTHANDLER], REPO, 2400)\n    print(\"\\n\".join((t.stdout + t.stderr).splitlines()[-5:]))\n    if t.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: pytest\"); ok = False\n    w = _run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\", \"-p\", \"no:cacheprovider\", \"-o\", FAULTHANDLER],\n             REPO / \"pathwidth_solver\", 2400)\n    print(\"\\n\".join((w.stdout + w.stderr).splitlines()[-3:]))\n    if w.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: pathwidth_solver pytest\"); ok = False\n    # The paper must build cleanly: no undefined references or citations.\n    m = subprocess.run([\"make\", \"check\"], cwd=PAPER, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join((m.stdout + m.stderr).splitlines()[-3:]))\n    if m.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: paper1/latex make check\"); ok = False\n    # Paper 3 (loop0015): same check, once its Makefile exists.\n    if (PAPER3 / \"Makefile\").exists():\n        m3 = subprocess.run([\"make\", \"check\"], cwd=PAPER3, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n        print(\"\\n\".join((m3.stdout + m3.stderr).splitlines()[-3:]))\n        if m3.returncode != 0:\n            print(\"GATE FAIL: paper3/latex make check\"); ok = False\n        # The owner's title, verbatim: the source carries it as `\\title{... $2^n$ ...}` and\n        # as the pdftitle; `$` and `\\ldots` are the only LaTeX in it (paper3/README.md).\n        main_tex = (PAPER3 / \"main.tex\").read_text() if (PAPER3 / \"main.tex\").exists() else \"\"\n        norm = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", main_tex.replace(\"$\", \"\").replace(\"\\\\ldots{}\", \"...\").replace(\"\\\\ldots\", \"...\"))\n        if TITLE not in norm:\n            print(\"GATE FAIL: paper3/latex/main.tex does not carry the owner's title verbatim\"); ok = False\n    else:\n        print(\"paper3/latex/Makefile not present yet: paper 3 check skipped\")\n    # Nothing under solutions/ is ever written by this loop.\n    sol = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--\", \"solutions/\"], cwd=REPO,\n                         capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()\n    if sol:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: solutions/ changed:\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(sol.splitlines()[:10])); ok = False\n    print(\"GATE PASS\" if ok else \"GATE FAIL\")\n    return 0 if ok else 1\n\n\n\n\ndef main() -> int:  # added 2026-11-02: a hung pytest (libgomp fork deadlock) held loop0012's gate for 13 h\n    try:\n        return _main()\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:\n        tail = \"\\n\".join((e.output or \"\").splitlines()[-40:])\n        print(f\"GATE FAIL: timeout in {e.cmd}\\n{tail}\")\n        return 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n=== audit heads\n# Statement audit: `exact_count_and_sat` (openai/math family 378, \"The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False\")\n\nAudited 2026-11-05 against the read-only clone at `/home/al/dev/untrusted/openai-math`\n(comparator file `lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean`, 220 lines; `S:` below\nmeans that file, `Sol:` the solution tree `lean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/`).\nNothing under the clone was executed. Mathlib definitions were read from our own copy\n(`/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/.lake/packages/mathlib`, rev `1192d62`) and re-read at the clone's\npinned revision `d13f23b7` (`lean/lake-manifest.json:11`) from raw.githubusercontent.com;\nthey agree verbatim. One Lean file of my own (`VarCheck.lean`, here) was compiled with our\ntoolchain to check a variable-inclusion question; one Python script (`check_encoding.py`)\ncomputes `L` and `runtimeScale`.\n\n---\n# Audit of the PROOF of `exact_count_and_sat` (openai/math family 378)\n\nScope: the Lean proof of `OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.exact_count_and_sat`\nin the read-only clone `/home/al/dev/untrusted/openai-math` (all paths below are relative\nto its `lean/` directory). Method: inspection only — `grep`/`sed`/`python3 -I` over the\nsources, and two web lookups (the Mathlib commit page, the comparator README). Nothing in\nthe clone was built, run, imported or evaluated. The companion audit of the STATEMENT is\nnot duplicated: the comparator statement is taken as written. Scripts:\n`closure.py` (import closure, nested-comment stripper, keyword grep; outputs\n`closure_modules.json`, `hits.json`) and `defdiff.py` (definition diff), both in this directory.\n\n## Verdict\n=== refs keys\n17:@misc{OAI:The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026,\n26:@article{ImpagliazzoPaturi2001,\n36:@article{ImpagliazzoPaturiZane2001,\n51:@misc{SienickiSienicki2026,\n68:@misc{LeanComparator,\n84:@misc{Nanoda,\n96:@misc{Lean4Export,\n104:@misc{Landrun,\n122:@techreport{Dinur2016,\n132:@inproceedings{ManurangsiRaghavendra2017,\n145:@article{Chalermsook2020,\n155:@inproceedings{Carmosino2016,\n166:@article{Dell2014,\n177:@article{Cygan2016,\n187:@inproceedings{Williams2016,\n210:@inproceedings{Biere2024CaDiCaL,\n224:@inproceedings{Ignatiev2018PySAT,\n238:@inproceedings{Sharma2019Ganak,\n249:@inproceedings{Chakraborty2013ApproxMC,\n262:@inproceedings{Soos2019BIRD,\n273:@article{Selman1996Hard,\n285:@article{Mertens2006Threshold,\n=== labels\n\\label{app:lean} \\label{app:tech} \\label{app:tech-definitions} \\label{app:tech-hypotheses} \\label{app:tech-keywords} \\label{app:tech-scaling} \\label{app:tech-spine} \\label{app:t