anion Lean of Section~\\ref{sec:lean}: the two files, the","+  axiom audit that prints the axioms of every declaration the paper","+  names (\\repofile{paper3/lean/axiom_check.lean}) with its committed","+  output, and the byte-level re-diff of the copied model against the","+  clone (\\repofile{paper3/lean/rediff.log}); Appendix~\\ref{app:lean}","+  lists the names;","+\\item the measurement of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}: every call's","+  seconds and result (\\repofile{paper3/latex/tables/practitioner_raw.csv}),","+  the versions, machine and load of the run of record","+  (\\repofile{paper3/latex/tables/practitioner_meta.json}), and the","+  script that regenerates the formulas from their seeds and re-runs it;","+\\item the two audits the paper rests on, with their scripts and the","+  committed text extract of the manuscript","+  (\\repofile{reports/scratch/eth_audit/}), and the four public texts","+  Section~\\ref{sec:related} quotes, as fetched, with their hashes","+  (\\repofile{paper3/related/fetched/});","+\\item the record of every question the writing could not settle, one","+  numbered entry each (\\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD}), and the","+  report of the blind reading of the whole paper against its sources","+  (\\repofile{paper3/refuter/}).","+\\end{itemize}","+The object of the paper is not ours. The OpenAI collection is read-only","+at commit \\texttt{4eaee875} of \\url{https://github.com/openai/math}","+(Apache-2.0 licence); the challenge file, the solution tree, the scope","+note and the manuscript are cited from it by file and line, and nothing","+in it was modified. A reader who wants to repeat the replay needs the","+collection at that commit, the pinned Lean release and the Mathlib","+revision Section~\\ref{sec:replay} names, a sandbox such as the one the","+scripts use, and about an hour of eight cores.","+","+\\paragraph{What this does not claim.} The statement above says what is","+available and how it is checked, not that every reader will see the","+same seconds: the timings of Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner} and the","+replay's 33 minutes are one machine's, and only the counts, the hashes","+and the axiom lines are expected to repeat exactly."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec12_ack.tex","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":46,"lines":["-% Acknowledgements, with the disclosure of AI use in paper 1's form (item 11).","+% Acknowledgements, with the disclosure of AI use in paper 1's form","+% (paper1/latex/sec8_ack.tex), written by item 11 on 2026-11-05. The","+% software versions are those the sections record (Section 5 the replay,","+% Section 7 the measurement, Section 8 our library)."," \\section*{Acknowledgements}"," \\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Acknowledgements}"," ","-\\placeholder{Item 11 writes the acknowledgements, with the disclosure of AI","-use in the form of \\repofile{paper1/latex/sec8_ack.tex}.}","+\\paragraph{Use of AI tools.} Much of this work was carried out with Claude","+Code (Anthropic), an AI coding assistant running Claude models. Under the","+author's direction it wrote the scripts, the companion Lean files and the","+drafts of the text, ran the sandboxed replay and the measurement, read","+the manuscript and the Lean sources, and searched the few texts","+Section~\\ref{sec:related} names. The author chose the question, fixed","+the title and the stance, directed the work, read the results and takes","+full responsibility for the content of this paper. We did not take the","+AI's word for any result. The verified statement is what the Lean kernel","+and, in our replay, a second checker written independently of Lean","+accept (Section~\\ref{sec:replay}); every number in the paper is printed","+by a script that a reader can run (the data statement above); every","+quotation carries the page and line, or the file and line, where it can","+be read; and the whole paper was read once more, against the clone, the","+extract, the audits and the logs, by a second session of the same","+assistant that had seen none of the drafts' sources, whose findings and","+what was done about each are on record","+(\\repofile{paper3/refuter/README.md}). ``People who checked'', in","+Section~\\ref{sec:intro}, means the author and that assistant.","+","+\\paragraph{The object of the paper.} The theorem, the proof and the","+manuscript this paper reads are OpenAI's","+\\citep{OAI:The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026},","+published under the Apache-2.0 licence in a collection whose checking","+tool \\citep{LeanComparator} and scope notes made the exact reading","+possible. Nothing in this paper is a claim of a flaw in that work.","+","+\\paragraph{Software.} The replay used the Lean release the collection","+pins, Lean~4.34.1 \\citep{MouraUllrich2021}, with the Mathlib library","+\\citep{Mathlib2020} at the revision the collection pins, inside the","+\\texttt{bwrap} sandbox Section~\\ref{sec:replay} describes; the second","+checker was \\texttt{nanoda\\_lib} \\citep{Nanoda} on an export written by","+\\texttt{lean4export} \\citep{Lean4Export}. Our own library builds with","+Lean~4.34.0-rc2 and Mathlib (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}). The measurement","+used CaDiCaL~1.9.5 \\citep{Biere2024CaDiCaL} through PySAT","+\\citep{Ignatiev2018PySAT}, Ganak~2.8.0 \\citep{Sharma2019Ganak} and","+ApproxMC~4.4.0 \\citep{Chakraborty2013ApproxMC, Soos2019BIRD}. The","+bibliography's DOIs were checked against Crossref and DataCite","+(\\repofile{paper3/latex/doi_check.log})."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/refs.bib","hunks":[{"oldStart":293,"oldLines":3,"newStart":293,"newLines":26,"lines":["   note    = {Venue from memory; DOI checked against Crossref on 2026-11-05 (item 10, \\texttt{paper3/scripts/check\\_refs.py}). Puts the 3-SAT threshold at $4.2667$},","   doi       = {10.1002/rsa.20090}"," }","+","+% Lean 4 and Mathlib, copied from paper1/latex/refs.bib (item 11, 2026-11-05)","+% for the ack